"name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[3,8]},{"id":"remaliah_2420","name":"Remaliah","also":"","summary":"Adorned by the Lord, the father of Pekah, who conspired successfully against Pekahiah (2 Kings 15:25, 27, 30, 32, 37; Isa. 7:1, 4, 5, 9; 8:6).","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"pekah_2299","name":"Pekah","also":"","summary":"Open-eyed, the son of Remaliah a captain in the army of Pekahiah, king of Israel, whom he slew, with the aid of a band of Gileadites, and succeeded (B.C. 758) on the throne (2 Kings 15:25).","verses":11,"father":"Remaliah","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[7,12]},{"id":"azrikam_566","name":"Azrikam","also":"","summary":"David his father.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"elkanah_1174","name":"Elkanah","also":"","summary":"The husband of Hannah.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"maaseiah_1852","name":"Maaseiah","also":"","summary":"Son of Ahaz. killed by Zichri.","verses":1,"father":"Ahaz","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"zichri_3074","name":"Zichri","also":"","summary":"One of' Dat-id's Worthies.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"oded_2237","name":"Oded","also":"","summary":"A prophet in the time of Ahaz and Pekah (2 Chr. 28:9-15).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"amasa_208","name":"Amasa","also":"","summary":"A son of Hadlai, and chief of Ephraim (2 Chr. 28:12) in the reign of Ahaz.","verses":1,"father":"Hadlai","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"azariah_386","name":"Azariah","also":"","summary":"Leader in Ephraim.","verses":1,"father":"Johanan","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"berechiah_473","name":"Berechiah","also":"","summary":"One of the seven Ephraimite chieftains, son of Meshillemoth (2 Chr. 28:12).","verses":1,"father":"Meshillemoth","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"hadlai_1344","name":"Hadlai","also":"","summary":"Resting, an Ephraimite; the father of Amasa, mentioned in 2 Chr. 28:12.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"jehizkiah_781","name":"Jehizkiah","also":"","summary":"Jehovah strengthens, one of the chiefs of Ephraim (2 Chr. 28:12).","verses":1,"father":"Shallum","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"johanan_1672","name":"Johanan","also":"","summary":"Your son name was Azariah.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"meshillemoth_2018","name":"Meshillemoth","also":"","summary":"The father of Berechiah (2 Chr. 28:12).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"shallum_2521","name":"Shallum","also":"","summary":"An Ephraimite chief (2 Chr. 28:12).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"tilgath-pilneser_2376","name":"Tilgath-pilneser","also":"Pul, Jareb","summary":"An Assyrian king. It has been a question whether he was identical with Tiglath-pileser III., or was his predecessor. The weight of evidence is certainly in favour of their identity.","verses":6,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"hezekiah_1512","name":"Hezekiah","also":"Ezekias","summary":"Son of Ahaz (2 Kings 18:1; 2 Chr. 29:1), whom he succeeded on the throne of the kingdom of Judah. He reigned twenty-nine years (B.C. 726-697).","verses":116,"father":"Ahaz","mother":"Abijah","v":[27]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,10,24,27]},{"id":"valley_of_the_son_of_hinnom_1226","name":"valley of the son of Hinnom","kind":"Valley","lat":31.76908,"lon":35.22799,"summary":"","verses":8,"v":[3]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[5,23]},{"id":"syria_1122","name":"Syria","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":37.5,"lon":37.5,"summary":"(Heb. Aram), the name in the Old Testament given to the whole country which lay to the north-east of Phoenicia, extending to beyond the Euphrates and the Tigris.","verses":64,"v":[5,23]},{"id":"samaria_1022","name":"Samaria","kind":"Region","lat":32.33142,"lon":35.22859,"summary":"A watch-mountain or a watch-tower. In the heart of the mountains of Israel, a few miles north-west of Shechem, stands the “hill of Shomeron,” a solitary mountain, a great “mamelon.”","verses":114,"v":[8,9,15]},{"id":"jericho_634","name":"Jericho","kind":"City","lat":31.87005,"lon":35.44388,"summary":"Place of fragrance, a fenced city in the midst of a vast grove of palm trees, in the plain of Jordan, over against the place where that river was crossed by the Israelites (Josh. 3:16).","verses":58,"v":[15]},{"id":"assyria_111","name":"Assyria","kind":"Region","lat":36.50969,"lon":43.2282,"summary":"The name derived from the city Asshur on the Tigris, the original capital of the country, was originally a colony from Babylonia, and was ruled by viceroys from that kingdom.","verses":116,"v":[16,20,21]},{"id":"aijalon_40","name":"Aijalon","kind":"City","lat":31.84488,"lon":35.03127,"summary":"A city in the tribe of Zebulun (Judg. 12:12), the modern Jalun, three miles north of Cabul.","verses":9,"v":[18]},{"id":"beth-shemesh_234","name":"Beth-shemesh","kind":"City","lat":31.73072,"lon":34.99293,"summary":"A sacerdotal city in the tribe of Dan (Josh. 21:16; 1 Sam. 6:15), on the north border of Judah (Josh. 15:10). It was the scene of an encounter between Jehoash, king of Israel, and Amaziah, king of Judah, in which the latter was made prisoner (2 Kings 14:11, 13).","verses":17,"v":[18]},{"id":"gederoth_453","name":"Gederoth","kind":"","lat":31.82334,"lon":34.77778,"summary":"","verses":2,"v":[18]},{"id":"gimzo_480","name":"Gimzo","kind":"City","lat":31.92866,"lon":34.94322,"summary":"A place fertile in sycamores, a city in the plain of Judah, the villages of which were seized by the Philistines (2 Chr. 28:18).","verses":1,"v":[18]},{"id":"negeb_885","name":"Negeb","kind":"Region","lat":30.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Heb. Negeb, that arid district to the south of Palestine through which lay the caravan route from Central Palestine to Egypt (Gen. 12:9; 13:1, 3; 46:1-6).","verses":36,"v":[18]},{"id":"shephelah_1074","name":"Shephelah","kind":"Region","lat":31.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"region","verses":6,"v":[18]},{"id":"timnah_1164","name":"Timnah","kind":"City","lat":31.78437,"lon":34.90968,"summary":"A town of Judah (Josh. 15:10). The Philistines took possession of it in the days of Ahaz (2 Chr. 28:18). It was about 20 miles west of Jerusalem.","verses":8,"v":[18]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[271,6242,6242,1121,1121,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,3389,3389,8337,8141,1732,1732,1732,1,1,3808,3808,3808,6213,3477,3477,3477,5869,5869,5869,3068,3068,3068],[1980,1980,1980,1870,1870,1870,4428,4428,4428,3478,3478,1571,1571,6213,4541,4541,1168,1168,1168],[1931,1931,6999,6999,1516,1516,1516,2011,2011,1197,1197,1121,1121,784,784,784,8441,8441,8441,8441,1471,1471,1471,834,3068,3068,3423,3423,3423,6440,1121,1121],[2076,2076,2076,6999,6999,6999,1116,1116,1116,1116,5921,1389,1389,8478,8478,3605,7488,6086],[3068,3068,3068,430,430,5414,5414,3027,3027,3027,4428,4428,4428,758,758,5221,5221,0,7617,7617,1419,7633,1834,1834,1571,1571,1571,5414,3027,3027,3027,4428,4428,4428,3478,3478,5221,5221,0,1419,1419,4347],[259,25